1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
You're sending me away to Saga?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
That's right. It's where Master Hebea was born.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
If I'm not mistaken, I believe that his wife passed away a long time ago,

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
so it should be quite a peaceful arrangement.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Honestly, I'm relieved.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Up against him, even the most notable dignitaries won't make a fuss.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
He has wisdom and experience on his side,

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
and, well, you would know more about these matters than I could explain.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Proprietor, Madam, you have my thanks. I appreciate all that you've done.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
In my years, I've never seen a courtesan like you before, Yugiiri.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
And I'm afraid we never will again.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
To gain so much popularity, she could no longer get customers? Unheard of.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
I'm sorry if I have caused you any trouble.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
I wish you the best life.

15
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
But knowing you, I shouldn't have cause to worry.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Oh my goodness, what have you girls been doing?

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Yugiiri, are you leaving us? Will we see you again? Is Saga really far away?

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Please don't go. I wanted you to teach me more about singing and dancing.

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
There, there, girls. She's a legendary courtesan who's starting a new life for herself.

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
You should be happy for her.

21
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Come now. Don't cry. Now. Let me see you smile.

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:38,000
I may be far away in Saga, but I promise that each of you will remain close to my heart.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Well, technically, Saga doesn't actually exist anymore.

24
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Huh?

25
00:03:13,962 --> 00:03:37,122
Don't Lady Yugiri always look so beautiful?

26
00:03:37,122 --> 00:03:38,482
Of course she does.

27
00:03:38,602 --> 00:03:40,002
She's a legendary courtesan.

28
00:03:40,282 --> 00:03:41,462
What makes her so legendary?

29
00:03:41,922 --> 00:03:43,242
You're too young to understand.

30
00:03:43,242 --> 00:03:51,802
Several months had passed since the legendary courtesan reluctantly left her old life.

31
00:03:53,062 --> 00:04:00,302
However, Master Hebeah, the high-ranking government official who arranged her freedom, passed away due to sudden illness.

32
00:04:01,702 --> 00:04:05,282
In accordance with his wishes, she was granted a portion of his fortune.

33
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:15,642
Despite the security her inheritance lent her, she faced the unfortunate prospect of living out the rest of her life in a town where she knew no one, and no one knew her.

34
00:04:15,642 --> 00:04:22,682
They don't call her a legend without good reason.

35
00:04:22,982 --> 00:04:26,162
I bet that girl puts the folks over in Kamiyashi-shou to shame.

36
00:04:26,822 --> 00:04:29,162
Why would she leave that lifestyle behind?

37
00:04:29,382 --> 00:04:30,202
Fresh treats!

38
00:04:30,302 --> 00:04:31,182
Come on by!

39
00:04:31,342 --> 00:04:33,042
Shirako, Manju, and Dango!

40
00:04:33,802 --> 00:04:35,202
Step right up and enjoy!

41
00:04:35,202 --> 00:04:41,442
Listen up, everyone!

42
00:04:41,882 --> 00:04:43,902
The time has come for us to take a stand!

43
00:04:43,982 --> 00:04:45,922
We must bring back Saga right now!

44
00:04:46,422 --> 00:04:46,822
Saga!

45
00:04:47,302 --> 00:04:47,742
Saga!

46
00:04:48,262 --> 00:04:48,702
Huh?

47
00:04:50,702 --> 00:04:51,962
What a creep.

48
00:04:52,282 --> 00:04:52,942
Let's go.

49
00:04:52,942 --> 00:04:55,702
Attention!

50
00:04:56,702 --> 00:04:58,842
Please stop by to watch our show!

51
00:05:00,982 --> 00:05:03,202
It's the Shingoro Traveling Show!

52
00:05:03,562 --> 00:05:05,302
We're only in town for seven days!

53
00:05:05,382 --> 00:05:05,642
Saga!

54
00:05:05,982 --> 00:05:06,282
Saga!

55
00:05:07,182 --> 00:05:08,802
Here, please take one, sir!

56
00:05:09,182 --> 00:05:09,662
Saga!

57
00:05:10,002 --> 00:05:11,542
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

58
00:05:14,782 --> 00:05:15,662
I'm sorry!

59
00:05:15,662 --> 00:05:15,822
I'm sorry!

60
00:05:15,822 --> 00:05:24,502
Watch where you're going!

61
00:05:24,942 --> 00:05:26,062
I'm sorry!

62
00:05:26,262 --> 00:05:26,902
I'm sorry!

63
00:05:29,042 --> 00:05:35,182
I see you're outspreading propaganda again!

64
00:05:35,682 --> 00:05:37,382
This time, you're coming with me!

65
00:05:37,642 --> 00:05:38,922
Stop struggling!

66
00:05:42,982 --> 00:05:45,222
Think I'll hold on to this for now.

67
00:05:45,822 --> 00:05:52,362
Kiiichi Momazaki, why are you always out here causing me so much damned trouble?

68
00:05:52,822 --> 00:05:55,602
Give it a rest before I haul you off to jail once and for all!

69
00:05:55,742 --> 00:05:58,502
I just want the people to remember how Saga used to be!

70
00:05:58,582 --> 00:05:59,282
Stop that thief!

71
00:05:59,602 --> 00:06:00,202
He's getting away!

72
00:06:00,582 --> 00:06:02,402
Don't move a muscle until I get back!

73
00:06:03,542 --> 00:06:04,342
I'm coming!

74
00:06:08,342 --> 00:06:08,822
Huh?

75
00:06:09,622 --> 00:06:09,942
Oh.

76
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,202
Thank you, Ito.

77
00:06:12,902 --> 00:06:13,942
Yeah, sure.

78
00:06:13,942 --> 00:06:15,942
You just never learn, do you?

79
00:06:16,902 --> 00:06:22,922
During that time, the members of the Meiji government considered Saga to be a problematic prefecture.

80
00:06:23,862 --> 00:06:31,582
And in the Bakumatsu period, it underwent westernization faster than other domains, making Saga a key location during the Reformation.

81
00:06:31,582 --> 00:06:39,122
But, with uprisings by the former samurai class during Meiji 7 and the accompanying defeats, its glory was tarnished.

82
00:06:39,122 --> 00:06:45,542
By Meiji 9, Saga had been divided up between two prefectures, Mizuma and Nagasaki.

83
00:06:46,202 --> 00:06:49,262
This resulted in its total erasure from the map.

84
00:06:49,262 --> 00:06:52,902
You need to stop getting into trouble.

85
00:06:54,162 --> 00:06:57,462
One day you're going to get yourself in it bad, and I won't be there to help you.

86
00:06:57,902 --> 00:06:59,042
I can't just stop.

87
00:06:59,282 --> 00:07:00,582
I want Saga back.

88
00:07:00,982 --> 00:07:02,122
The way it used to be.

89
00:07:02,982 --> 00:07:06,282
You're never going to accomplish anything if you keep doing this by yourself.

90
00:07:06,642 --> 00:07:09,002
The Imperial Court still has their issues with Saga.

91
00:07:09,002 --> 00:07:14,262
On top of that, nobody wants a repeat of the Saga war.

92
00:07:14,722 --> 00:07:16,682
But I'm not trying to start a war!

93
00:07:17,102 --> 00:07:18,622
That's how it comes across.

94
00:07:19,262 --> 00:07:21,462
Let's say the Saga does get its name back.

95
00:07:22,162 --> 00:07:23,122
What happens after?

96
00:07:24,282 --> 00:07:26,162
I hadn't thought of...

97
00:07:26,162 --> 00:07:27,442
Alright, enough of that.

98
00:07:27,662 --> 00:07:30,062
Set aside the restoration of Saga, okay?

99
00:07:30,402 --> 00:07:32,122
Let's go check out the cherry blossoms.

100
00:07:32,662 --> 00:07:33,502
You'll love it.

101
00:07:33,882 --> 00:07:37,182
It'll make you forget all about that old Saga you're so fond of.

102
00:07:37,242 --> 00:07:37,582
Promise!

103
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:38,202
Huh?

104
00:07:39,002 --> 00:07:41,442
You know I'm not really interested in that kind of stuff.

105
00:07:43,602 --> 00:07:44,922
Hey, where's the meat?

106
00:07:45,702 --> 00:07:46,702
I ate it all.

107
00:07:47,402 --> 00:07:48,662
I'm going to get you!

108
00:07:49,022 --> 00:07:51,882
If you think you can take me on, you just try me!

109
00:07:52,362 --> 00:07:56,322
Teacher, you know, you would be the talk of the town if you weren't always cooped up in here.

110
00:07:56,502 --> 00:08:00,242
Plus, the cherry blossoms are in bloom, and I know where all the best viewing spots are.

111
00:08:04,282 --> 00:08:05,462
You're free now.

112
00:08:05,462 --> 00:08:07,982
You should explore the outside world.

113
00:08:07,982 --> 00:08:14,762
Wow, look at the battle!

114
00:08:14,762 --> 00:08:18,702
Wow, look at the battle!

115
00:08:18,702 --> 00:08:18,882
It's pretty!

116
00:08:18,882 --> 00:08:19,062
It's pretty!

117
00:08:19,062 --> 00:08:19,642
Huh?

118
00:08:19,642 --> 00:08:23,162
Hmm?

119
00:08:23,162 --> 00:08:23,902
Hmm.

120
00:08:23,902 --> 00:08:24,022
Hmm.

121
00:08:41,082 --> 00:08:41,322
Hmm.

122
00:08:41,422 --> 00:08:41,842
Hmm.

123
00:08:41,842 --> 00:08:42,382
Hmm.

124
00:08:42,382 --> 00:09:06,582
Oh, is this yours?

125
00:09:06,582 --> 00:09:10,382
Here.

126
00:09:10,382 --> 00:09:12,882
Thank you, it is.

127
00:09:12,882 --> 00:09:18,882
I bought it moments before.

128
00:09:18,882 --> 00:09:19,882
Coming through!

129
00:09:19,882 --> 00:09:21,882
Get out of the way!

130
00:09:21,882 --> 00:09:23,882
Look out!

131
00:09:37,882 --> 00:09:39,882
Please allow me to help you.

132
00:09:40,382 --> 00:09:48,882
Oh no, I'm…

133
00:09:48,882 --> 00:09:50,882
Here, use this.

134
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:52,882
Thank you very much.

135
00:09:52,882 --> 00:09:56,882
Hey, this is mine.

136
00:09:56,882 --> 00:10:01,382
I'm sorry, I had no idea.

137
00:10:01,382 --> 00:10:07,382
I apologize for treating it like tissue paper.

138
00:10:07,382 --> 00:10:19,882
You'll feel better once you change it to some dry clothes.

139
00:10:19,882 --> 00:10:22,382
Oh, what happened to you?

140
00:10:22,382 --> 00:10:24,382
She's an angel.

141
00:10:24,382 --> 00:10:26,382
Huh?

142
00:10:26,382 --> 00:10:28,382
I think I know who she is.

143
00:10:28,382 --> 00:10:32,882
If I'm right, she's the legendary courtesan who moved to Saga at the end of last year.

144
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:33,882
Legendary?

145
00:10:33,882 --> 00:10:34,882
Come on.

146
00:10:34,882 --> 00:10:36,882
You mean you haven't heard of her?

147
00:10:36,882 --> 00:10:38,882
Pay more attention to town gossip.

148
00:10:38,882 --> 00:10:43,382
She's a renowned courtesan named Yugiri.

149
00:10:43,382 --> 00:10:47,382
Her performances were unlike anything anyone in Edo had ever seen.

150
00:10:47,382 --> 00:10:48,882
Men and women alike revered her.

151
00:10:48,882 --> 00:10:53,882
Yugiri was in high demand to the point that her prices skyrocketed to an obscene amount.

152
00:10:53,882 --> 00:10:55,882
No one could afford her entertainment anymore.

153
00:10:55,882 --> 00:10:59,382
Leaders of the Restoration fought over her.

154
00:10:59,382 --> 00:11:02,382
And it's rumored that the Meiji court almost fell apart because of it.

155
00:11:02,382 --> 00:11:05,382
And now she lives in Saga?

156
00:11:05,382 --> 00:11:07,382
Don't fall in love.

157
00:11:07,382 --> 00:11:09,382
I'm not in love!

158
00:11:09,382 --> 00:11:12,382
You couldn't possibly handle a woman like that.

159
00:11:12,382 --> 00:11:14,382
She's from a different world.

160
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:20,382
Maybe I could learn more about her world.

161
00:11:20,382 --> 00:11:45,882
Maybe I could learn more about her world.

162
00:11:45,882 --> 00:11:57,342
Hello again.

163
00:11:57,342 --> 00:12:09,262
You didn't need to go through such trouble just for me.

164
00:12:09,262 --> 00:12:13,062
I know it's not much, but I wanted to say thank you for, uh...

165
00:12:13,062 --> 00:12:14,982
I am touched that you thought of me, though.

166
00:12:14,982 --> 00:12:19,202
Thank you, but you should run along home now.

167
00:12:19,202 --> 00:12:22,202
The people in town might get the wrong idea.

168
00:12:26,242 --> 00:12:30,882
But I don't care what they think.

169
00:12:30,882 --> 00:12:35,202
See, all this talk about you being from a different world,

170
00:12:35,202 --> 00:12:38,842
the complicated details about your history don't matter to me.

171
00:12:38,842 --> 00:12:42,162
In our saga, it'll be…

172
00:12:44,982 --> 00:12:49,202
Pardon me. Does a man by the name of Kiichi Momazaki live here?

173
00:12:49,202 --> 00:12:53,422
Uh…

174
00:12:53,422 --> 00:13:09,422
Pardon me. Does a man by the name of Kiichi Momazaki live here?

175
00:13:09,422 --> 00:13:27,642
It's Saga. I am Saga. No, Saga is me!

176
00:13:27,642 --> 00:13:34,862
Oh my! Are you all right, my lord?

177
00:13:34,862 --> 00:13:38,862
Grandpa, did you wander off?

178
00:13:38,862 --> 00:13:44,082
This is a remedy for colds and other illnesses.

179
00:13:44,082 --> 00:13:46,082
A very nourishing collection of herbs.

180
00:13:46,082 --> 00:13:49,082
I asked an old acquaintance to send it to me.

181
00:13:49,082 --> 00:13:51,082
That's so kind of you. Thank you.

182
00:13:51,082 --> 00:13:53,082
I was feeling a little guilty.

183
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:57,302
You braved that blazing sun just to bring me a simple gift of gratitude.

184
00:13:57,302 --> 00:14:01,302
It's nothing. Besides, I wanted to do it.

185
00:14:01,302 --> 00:14:03,302
It was so thoughtful.

186
00:14:03,302 --> 00:14:07,302
Since I arrived in Saga, you're the first one to come calling,

187
00:14:07,302 --> 00:14:09,302
other than my dance students.

188
00:14:09,302 --> 00:14:13,802
I must apologize for my grandpa earlier.

189
00:14:13,802 --> 00:14:16,302
He's a little unwell.

190
00:14:16,302 --> 00:14:20,182
He seemed like an interesting man to me.

191
00:14:20,182 --> 00:14:22,842
He was already on the decline.

192
00:14:22,842 --> 00:14:26,762
But I think when Saga lost its name, he got even worse.

193
00:14:26,762 --> 00:14:30,822
He started ranting some nonsense about how he'd be able to raise the dead

194
00:14:30,822 --> 00:14:34,702
if only he had his old powers back.

195
00:14:34,702 --> 00:14:39,942
About eight years ago, a big battle took place right here in Saga,

196
00:14:39,942 --> 00:14:43,282
and my father was killed.

197
00:14:43,282 --> 00:14:46,242
After that, I had no place to go.

198
00:14:46,242 --> 00:14:49,542
I spent my days cowering in the wilderness.

199
00:14:49,542 --> 00:14:54,262
I don't know what would have happened if Gramps hadn't found me.

200
00:14:54,262 --> 00:14:57,302
I owe him more than I could ever give him.

201
00:14:57,302 --> 00:14:59,342
The only thing he cares about,

202
00:14:59,342 --> 00:15:02,042
the only thing he wants in return,

203
00:15:02,042 --> 00:15:04,302
is for me to save Saga.

204
00:15:04,302 --> 00:15:07,342
At first, I was confused by what that meant.

205
00:15:07,342 --> 00:15:10,182
But then, when Saga lost its name,

206
00:15:10,182 --> 00:15:14,442
it felt like everything my father died trying to protect slipped away.

207
00:15:14,442 --> 00:15:17,642
And Saga might vanish from people's hearts, too.

208
00:15:17,642 --> 00:15:20,362
But I couldn't let that happen.

209
00:15:20,362 --> 00:15:24,442
I think that fate is responsible for bringing my grandpa and I together,

210
00:15:24,442 --> 00:15:27,202
so that I could find my purpose in life.

211
00:15:30,202 --> 00:15:33,182
Yugiri, from this day forward,

212
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:36,222
this is where you'll be living.

213
00:15:36,222 --> 00:15:41,982
Finally, I have a clear vision for the future.

214
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:45,162
I know in my heart what I want to do now.

215
00:15:45,162 --> 00:15:47,822
I want to create a new Saga.

216
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:52,702
A place where it doesn't matter what your status is or who you were before.

217
00:15:52,702 --> 00:15:55,922
A place where anyone can choose their own paths in life,

218
00:15:55,922 --> 00:15:58,542
and they can stay true to themselves.

219
00:15:58,542 --> 00:15:59,582
Mm.

220
00:15:59,582 --> 00:16:00,802
I see.

221
00:16:00,802 --> 00:16:03,762
That sounds like a beautiful place to live.

222
00:16:07,762 --> 00:16:09,422
Take one!

223
00:16:09,422 --> 00:16:11,102
Please take one, sir!

224
00:16:11,102 --> 00:16:12,382
You there!

225
00:16:12,382 --> 00:16:14,062
You want to get arrested?

226
00:16:15,742 --> 00:16:17,182
Very funny!

227
00:16:17,182 --> 00:16:19,182
You never give up, do you?

228
00:16:23,182 --> 00:16:25,682
Um, Yugiri helped me out some.

229
00:16:25,682 --> 00:16:27,682
Fixing the composition and stuff.

230
00:16:29,982 --> 00:16:32,282
Oh, haha, there, there.

231
00:16:32,282 --> 00:16:34,282
There, it's okay.

232
00:16:34,282 --> 00:16:35,582
Don't cry.

233
00:16:47,182 --> 00:16:54,182
I'm here with our dinner.

234
00:16:54,182 --> 00:16:56,182
I'm here with our dinner.

235
00:16:58,602 --> 00:17:00,202
Do forgive me, sir.

236
00:17:00,202 --> 00:17:03,702
I felt an eerie presence, and perhaps I'm a little unnerved.

237
00:17:03,702 --> 00:17:05,702
I'm so sorry!

238
00:17:05,702 --> 00:17:07,542
I know I'm running late.

239
00:17:07,542 --> 00:17:08,442
Huh?

240
00:17:08,442 --> 00:17:11,202
Yito, you came early.

241
00:17:11,202 --> 00:17:14,962
I guess I couldn't wait to meet the legendary courtesan, Yugiri.

242
00:17:14,962 --> 00:17:17,502
Look, this big one is for you.

243
00:17:17,502 --> 00:17:19,062
So huge!

244
00:17:19,062 --> 00:17:21,602
You actually caught that thing in the Fukushoe River?

245
00:17:21,602 --> 00:17:22,562
Wow!

246
00:17:40,862 --> 00:17:41,862
Tasty!

247
00:17:41,862 --> 00:17:45,402
I see your exceptional skills extend to cooking, as well.

248
00:17:45,402 --> 00:17:50,282
The man who arranged my freedom for me taught me all kinds of new talents.

249
00:17:50,282 --> 00:17:53,202
They've helped me to live in the outside world since.

250
00:17:53,202 --> 00:17:55,202
Hmm.

251
00:17:55,202 --> 00:17:56,202
I bet he did.

252
00:17:59,622 --> 00:18:01,422
Perhaps you should do the same.

253
00:18:01,422 --> 00:18:02,422
Same what?

254
00:18:02,422 --> 00:18:06,102
I mean, it's never a bad idea to learn new skills.

255
00:18:06,102 --> 00:18:08,262
You could become a scholar or a doctor.

256
00:18:08,262 --> 00:18:12,142
If you really want to help people, you should focus on realistic goals,

257
00:18:12,142 --> 00:18:15,782
instead of wasting your time trying to bring back the glory days of Saga.

258
00:18:23,862 --> 00:18:26,162
You happened upon this nice lady.

259
00:18:26,162 --> 00:18:27,782
Maybe it was a sign.

260
00:18:27,782 --> 00:18:28,782
You know?

261
00:18:28,782 --> 00:18:31,022
Maybe it's time for you to start a family.

262
00:18:31,022 --> 00:18:32,022
Huh?

263
00:18:32,022 --> 00:18:35,562
Being the head of a household gives a man a feeling of responsibility.

264
00:18:35,562 --> 00:18:37,022
Don't you want that?

265
00:18:37,022 --> 00:18:38,562
the game?

266
00:18:38,562 --> 00:18:39,562
Huh?

267
00:18:41,622 --> 00:18:43,562
No way!

268
00:18:43,562 --> 00:18:44,722
Are you stupid!?

269
00:18:44,722 --> 00:18:46,262
Seriously, what are you saying?

270
00:18:46,262 --> 00:18:48,402
Why on earth made you say something so crazy?

271
00:18:50,362 --> 00:18:55,282
Oh my.

272
00:18:55,282 --> 00:18:58,942
Are you alright?

273
00:18:58,942 --> 00:19:00,942
Right? Lord Kiichi?

274
00:19:02,382 --> 00:19:04,542
He's always been such a lightweight.

275
00:19:08,782 --> 00:19:09,982
That's all right.

276
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:15,182
Have one with me.

277
00:19:15,182 --> 00:19:17,102
No, I'm fine.

278
00:19:24,462 --> 00:19:25,902
Tell me, Lord Ito,

279
00:19:25,902 --> 00:19:29,262
just how long have you and Lord Kiichi known each other?

280
00:19:29,262 --> 00:19:31,742
We only met two years ago.

281
00:19:31,742 --> 00:19:36,222
I heard about some oddball who was passing out strange pamphlets in the streets.

282
00:19:36,222 --> 00:19:38,542
I was amused at first.

283
00:19:38,542 --> 00:19:40,542
People seemed to ignore him,

284
00:19:40,542 --> 00:19:43,582
walking right past him as if he weren't there.

285
00:19:43,582 --> 00:19:45,182
Yet he never gave up.

286
00:19:45,182 --> 00:19:47,342
He was so determined.

287
00:19:47,342 --> 00:19:50,462
There had to be better ways to get the word out, but

288
00:19:50,462 --> 00:19:52,862
to be honest, he's a fool.

289
00:19:56,782 --> 00:20:00,462
This country's changed, and it's going to keep changing fast.

290
00:20:01,502 --> 00:20:04,302
Nothing good will ever come of clinging to history.

291
00:20:04,942 --> 00:20:08,382
I don't think Kiichi has any interest in bringing back the past.

292
00:20:09,262 --> 00:20:11,662
He wants to create a more progressive saga.

293
00:20:14,222 --> 00:20:16,782
It might be nothing more than a fantasy right now,

294
00:20:16,782 --> 00:20:22,382
but he wants it, and I think that I want it too, to live in that saga.

295
00:20:31,102 --> 00:20:35,342
Sooner or later, reality will set in, and he's going to get his heart broken.

296
00:20:36,222 --> 00:20:38,222
This country isn't ready for that saga.

297
00:20:39,262 --> 00:20:39,742
Not yet.

298
00:20:42,062 --> 00:20:43,342
Thank you for this.

299
00:20:43,342 --> 00:20:52,222
It was enlightening.

300
00:20:56,942 --> 00:20:58,222
Please take one!

301
00:20:58,222 --> 00:21:00,222
For Saga!

302
00:21:00,222 --> 00:21:10,142
Sir, could you tell us more about the information in this handout?

303
00:21:10,142 --> 00:21:12,382
We're after the same things that you are.

304
00:21:12,382 --> 00:21:14,222
The old saga.

305
00:21:14,222 --> 00:21:25,502
Those videos are there for the fact that you have this to match!

306
00:21:26,302 --> 00:21:29,582
So, are there sleeping things?

307
00:21:31,422 --> 00:21:33,342
Can you follow me unless I come out so,

308
00:21:35,182 --> 00:21:38,222
what can be shared in front of my ear?

309
00:21:38,222 --> 00:21:38,902
A default to her.

310
00:21:38,902 --> 00:21:39,742
Nothing.

311
00:21:39,742 --> 00:21:40,542
I'm thankful for this.

312
00:21:40,542 --> 00:22:10,522
Thank you.

313
00:23:24,922 --> 00:23:32,582
It's me, Yugiri. There's something truly inspiring about men willing to risk everything for their beliefs.

314
00:23:33,082 --> 00:23:39,842
Next time on Episode 9 of Zombieland Saga Revenge, The Saga Incident Part 2. This is goodbye.

